ave and noble when he agreed  to take responsibility for defeating  dobby but if this battle ends in dabi's  death then shoto will never be the same  again and neither will the story  personally i think that shotok killing  dobby or dobby dying in this fight as a  result of his own flames would be good  for the entire series i say that because  it would make the story feel darker and  more realistic  not every villain can be saved and if a  villain is out of control and determined  to keep hurting innocent people killing  him may be the only option and also a  necessity seeing shoto and the other  students having to come to terms with  this would add a new dimension to the  mha world and it would make everything  feel a lot more gritty and more real now  of course dobby could come back after  shoto's attack and kill shoto instead  but i don't see that happening shoto has  been through a lot to get here and he is  a fan favorite so if anyone dies in this  battle it will be dobby and if dobby  doesn't die and he ends up like atoning  for his sins somehow personally i think  that would be unrealistic given what we  know about his warped character but  we'll have to wait and see what do you  guys think did shoto just kill dabi or  will dabi survive this will shoto  eventually be forced to kill dobby or  will dabi kill shoto instead or do you  think that they could both survive this  fight definitely leave your thoughts  down in the comments below you know i  always love hearing from you if you're  interested in more mha content right now  check out my video on a potential mha  time skip link in the description don't  forget to leave a like to help out with  that youtube algorithm and of course if  you're not subscribed yet make this the  video that you subscribe and hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications you really have to go  through the trouble of subscribing  hitting that bell and then selecting the  option that says all if you don't do  that you'r